# The qcwcn HAL (vendor/lib64/libwifi-hal.so) loads and unloads the WLAN driver
# modules when it switches interface use cases, so it calls init_module() and
# delete_module(), which need CAP_SYS_MODULE. The service's rc already asks for
# SYS_MODULE, and system/sepolicy/private/hal_wifi.te grants net_admin and
# net_raw, but not sys_module, so every attempt was denied:
#
#   avc: denied { sys_module } for capability=16 scontext=u:r:hal_wifi_default:s0
#
# The HAL then failed the interface creation: the config netlink handler
# reported "Error code:-19 (No such device)", WifiChipAidlImpl returned
# WifiStatusCode::ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE, ClientModeManager never started, and Wi-Fi
# stayed off (which also hides the hotspot entry in Settings).
allow hal_wifi_default self:capability sys_module;
